A||||4||Wade87GT||Paid too much for rotors?||||5||
Z||000000||Wade87GT||12-31-2001||01:53 PM||||After going through most of the previous threads on brakes and rotors, I went with NAPA as the suggested source. New, precision made in the U.S. (no turning required) and they sure look nice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I've always had an excellent set-up using the stock system (plus carbomet pads) so I wanted to continue with that, this time adding Earl's S/S lines. But did I pay too much? The front hub/rotor was $81.49 each and they did not come with any bearings or seals (were they supposed to and will I now need to get them?). The rears cost $54.99 each, maybe because they were actually imported from Canada. I need start this job tomorrow and have it completed by Sunday so any info would be helpful. I also need to replace the master cylinder (have a rebuilt unit from Discount Auto Parts, some company starting with an A?), any tips on that? I wanted GM parts for everything but I couldn't get the correct part numbers to order them from gmpartsdirect.com, which I know would have saved me some money.<P>Thanks,<P>Wade<p>[This message has been edited by Wade87GT (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||x-thumpr-x||12-31-2001||02:17 PM||||Well, it sounds like you paid the right amount for the rotors. I paid just a little more for mine (Canadian cash$) and I've never seen the front rotors come with the bearings and seals. They do have the sleave for the bearing already in the rotors though. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||12-31-2001||02:37 PM||||Rotors usually don't come with seals or races. It usually is better to start out with a fresh set of both as the old ones have worn together. Make sure you pack the new bearings with grease and don't overtighten them or they wont last squat.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||12-31-2001||07:45 PM||||Prices sound quite reasonable actually.  The early Fiero front rotor is kind of a 'special' piece (hub too!)  Get new bearings/seals as well, get the BEST YOU CAN. Don't skimp here, belive me!<P><BR>PS: I just piad $160 for rotors! :S)  Of course, they were 2-piece 13" ventelated and cross-cast perforated.  For a 911-993 Twin Turbo.  So not too bad a deal really  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>(and yes, they're going on my Fiero. One way or another!)<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||rodmcneill||12-31-2001||09:57 PM||||I won some Bendix front rotors recently on E bay for $35 for the pair. I don't need them right now but that was too good a deal to pass up!||||reg||1
